<article class="env-lemma" id="0CUS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CUS">Lemma <span data-tag="0CUS">71.3.5</span>.</a> Let $K/k$ be a field extension. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $k$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $y \in X_ K$ with image $x \in X$. If $y$ is a weakly associated point of the pullback $\mathcal{F}_ K$, then $x$ is a weakly associated point of $\mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is the translation of Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CUC" data-tag="0CUC">31.6.5</a> into the language of algebraic spaces. We omit the details of the translation. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>